From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Modrinth Enhanced <patches@modrinth-enhanced.invalid>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:26:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Launch a running instance again on another account

An instance that is running can be started once more from the button
beside Stop on its page. The new copy runs as whichever account is
selected now, so switching accounts first is how one instance is played
on two accounts at once. A plain launch still refuses a running instance,
so a double-clicked play button stays one game.

The live log was kept per instance, so two copies would have written
into one buffer. It is kept per process now, log events carry the
process they came from, and while more than one copy runs the Logs tab
shows a console for each, named after its account. The instance's log
file is shared: another copy appends to it under a header naming its
account instead of wiping what the first is still writing.

The app event bindings are regenerated for the new log event field.

Adapted from Noctrinth (https://github.com/Everelsu/Noctrinth).
